From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flavius <Flavius256@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:18:00 +0000
Subject: unused parameters

Drop parameters the retail code never reads.

Each of these declared a parameter that the retail code never reads (it writes the register
first, or never touches it), so its callers looked one argument short to hostgen.

- FUN_L09_002efda8: the unused float angle parameter is gone. The function never reads it (no
  $f12 in the retail code); the one caller passes two arguments, and each call was reported as
  short of one.
- FUN_L16_002a0dc0: the unused float unused parameter is gone. The retail code writes $f12
  (neg.s $f12, $f13 at 0x2A0E8C) before it reads it; callers pass five arguments.
- relocate_asset_entry_pointers (FUN_002032e0): the unused third parameter (s32 on) is gone. The
  function reads only a0 and a1 (it sets a1 to 0 for its loop); every caller passes two, and
  each of 8 call sites was reported as short of one.
- transition_default_draw (FUN_001eb410): takes no parameter. The C had an unused_parameter;
  retail never reads a0 before it loads it (0x1EB42C), and transition_do_transition calls it
  with nothing.
- FUN_L00_002e83c0 (the camera lock): the unused second parameter is gone. The retail code
  writes a1 (lui $5, %hi(D_L00_0015EF50)) before it reads it; its callers pass one argument.
- FUN_002166e8, FUN_00205278, FUN_00204790: the unused parameters are gone ((void)). None of the
  three reads its argument registers (each writes a0/a1 first, or never touches them); callers
  that pass something are unaffected. The port's host/scene_start.c calls FUN_00204790 with
  nothing now.
